 example. Let\u2019s say we have a ONE side model, God. The MANY side model would be Human. Each God could have MANY Humans following him/her through a JOIN model of GuardianAngel. The God model could have many GuardianAngels but lets say s/he doesn\u2019t care about keeping track of all his/her follower Humans. Who said DB associations were boring?","topics":[],"score":1770},{"name":"tuckerd/list_it","owner":"tuckerd","html_url":"https://github.com/tuckerd/list_it","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":"Keep all of you grocery, hardware store... lists organized (CodeFellows - App A Day: Nested Resources)","topics":[],"score":1770},{"name":"dbsiegel/simple-cms","owner":"dbsiegel","html_url":"https://github.com/dbsiegel/simple-cms","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":"training in rails3","topics":[],"score":1770},{"name":"bvuongx/house_tweaker","owner":"bvuongx","html_url":"https://github.com/bvuongx/house_tweaker","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":1770},{"name":"bvuongx/assignment_tracker","owner":"bvuongx","html_url":"https://github.com/bvuongx/assignment_tracker","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":1770},{"name":"bvuongx/new_recipes","owner":"bvuongx","html_url":"https://github.com/bvuongx/new_recipes","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":"Final App of the day for Code Fellows silver.  Takes user input for recipes and ingredients.  Uses nested resources and twitter bootstrap.","topics":[],"score":1770},{"name":"bvuongx/Recipes_you_name_it","owner":"bvuongx","html_url":"https://github.com/bvuongx/Recipes_you_name_it","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score":1770},{"name":"bvuongx/Recipes","owner":"bvuongx","html_url":"https://github.com/bvuongx/Recipes","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Ruby","description":null,"topics":[],"score